se-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-9r[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Serialize bead-store writes with SDD sidecar integration[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Concurrent bead-store writers and SDD sidecar integration in the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]same clone can no longer wedge each other: `git rebase --continue` [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]is never fed a foreign un-staged worktree, a successful `rebase [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]--abort` is never escalated to `UNRECOVERABLE`, machine-managed [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]recovery never discards committed bead claims, and the recurring [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`sdd-sidecar` / `workspace_sdd_clone_recovery` axe error stops.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase/repos/plans/202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]sdd_clone_integration_race.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One critical section for bead mutation, commit, and [/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]integration[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]serialize[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'One critical section for bead mutation, commit, and integration' [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]section: put the bead-store worktree materialization and its git commit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]inside the same store-write-lock critical section that SDD integration [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]already uses, so a claim's un-staged JSONL can never land inside another[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]process's rebase.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rollback verification asserts only SASE-owned invariants[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]verify[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Rollback verification asserts only SASE-owned invariants' section: stop[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]treating a foreign worktree or untracked delta as proof that SASE broke [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the clone, so a clean `rebase --abort` reports the benign aborted status[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instead of escalating to `UNRECOVERABLE` and triggering destructive [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]recovery.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Conflict probes stop reporting git failures as \"no conflicts\"[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]probes[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Conflict probes stop reporting git failures as \"no conflicts\"' section:[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]make the unmerged-path and conflicted-file probes distinguish \"clean\" [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]from \"could not tell\", route the bead conflict resolver's probes through[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the shared git-lock retry policy, and stop rewriting every event stream [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]on every conflict.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Machine-managed SDD git ignores the user's rerere config[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]rerere[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Machine-managed SDD git ignores the user's rerere config' section: [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]disable rerere for every SASE-issued git command in a machine-managed [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]SDD store and purge the resolution cache that the user's global [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`rerere.autoupdate` already leaked into the shared plans clone.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bound repeated doomed integration attempts[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]backoff[dim] · [dim][/dim]after verify[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Bound repeated doomed integration attempts' section: add a per-clone [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]failed-integration cooldown so a clone that cannot rebase is not [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]re-rebased about once per second, and report the suppressed attempts [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instead of hiding them.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Worktree-mutating callers wait for the store write lock [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]instead of failing open[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]lockwait[dim] · [dim][/dim]after serialize[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Worktree-mutating callers wait for the store write lock instead of [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]failing open' section: keep fail-open only where it is safe, and make [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the paths that mutate a shared SDD worktree either wait long enough [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]under contention or fail closed.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reconcile the discarded claims and reap the recovery residue[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]repair[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Reconcile the discarded claims and reap the recovery residue' section: [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]audit every retained recovery ref and stash in the shared plans clone [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]for bead state that never reached the remote, reconcile what is still [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]live, and add bounded reaping so the residue does not accumulate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]forever.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Concurrent-writer soak exercise[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]soak[dim] · [dim][/dim]after serialize, verify, probes, rerere, backoff, lockwait[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Concurrent-writer soak exercise' section: drive many concurrent bead [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]claims against one clone while integration runs and assert no [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`UNRECOVERABLE` outcome, no discarded local commit, and no axe error [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]digest entry.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-9r","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","phase_bead_id":"sase-9r.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-c60f1dd98fbc8864126fb7f0a238f6b5","started_at":"2026-07-26T10:52:10.837964+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"ccb74ab23dc790dd9387dbf9d98428c400d7a7009a569bdb03a35746bfefca36","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-9r.8/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"345b6ae5d5638bad5c8403db2bc67a918cac7540ccfda476565efb8cce0235b1","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-9r.8/meta.json","size_bytes":603},"prompt":{"digest":"fc607c84f2bf792e779f49ab7a5bec4e3470471974a5638638e791fb959b1088","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-9r.8/prompt.md","size_bytes":299},"state":{"digest":"bfa1eb46a6652c2c0eae7603a3830997411cacdd9503ed0ebdad4c01c0e89efa","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-9r.8/state.json","size_bytes":163}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-9r.8","local_name":"sase-9r.8","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-9r","agent_clan_generation":"20260726065158","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-9r.8","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-9r","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","phase_bead_id":"sase-9r.8","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-ca119903b107a1abd6e68d0341d2be5d","started_at":"20260726065205","state":"waiting"},{"commits":[],"dismi